# p_9b3d — Hana's Commute Objects: Hook at the Door, Kitchen at Dinner

When Hana comes home from her office around 5:30 on a weekday, her commute objects go to the entry area in a predictable dump. The jacket and scarf hang on the entry hook. The keys, wallet, and sunglasses are set on the entry table. The laptop, water bottle, and pen are placed on the entry hook or table. The charger stays at the entry hook all day (it is always home, plugged in or set aside). But the water bottle is the exception: during dinner it migrates to the kitchen table, where Hana drinks while eating. The laptop and pen stay at the entry hook for the evening unless Hana does evening work at desk_b1. The jacket stays at the hook all evening.

This hypothesis is distinct from "The Entry Mess" (p_d3e8) in that it specifies the water bottle moves to the kitchen table during dinner (not staying at the hook), and it is distinct from "No Laptop Travel" (p_f5a0) in that the laptop IS out of the house during work hours and returns at 5:30. The day-0 evidence supports this: water_bottle_hana was at kitchen_table_k1 at 20:00 (not at the entry hook), and laptop_hana's most-seen location is entry_hook_e1. The "Entry Mess" document got mixed results (for 2, against 7 on the laptop at the hook), suggesting the laptop does end up at the hook but not always immediately.

